{"ts":"2026-08-13T08:45:58.302Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"7ebf2cca0e1c37e7b3d988ef","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-hnc9w7","lineage:pm-hnc9w7","lineage:pm-a8zm","lineage:pm-6x7o","lineage:pm-96h7","lineage:pm-33cw","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"pm-hnc9w7","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-hnc9w7","lineage:pm-hnc9w7","lineage:pm-a8zm","lineage:pm-6x7o","lineage:pm-96h7","lineage:pm-33cw","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.229","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-r3o7x4"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"The related ceiling is pinned to the live count with block enforcement, so recording one associative sibling relation anywhere in the tracker fails CI while the share floor it duplicates would have allowed it"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":""},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","assurance","governance","graph","ratchet"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-08-13T08:45:58.302Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-13T08:45:58.302Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":180},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Associative edge growth is governed by a composition ratio, so an addition that raises semantic share can never fail the associative bound; Any retained raw count bound declares explicit headroom and a rationale for the headroom, so it is not pinned to the observation that created it; A negative control proves the bound still fails an associative-only dilution pass and passes a mixed pass that raises semantic share; The two overlapping declarations are reconciled into one enforced quantity with the other demoted to reporting, recorded as a disposition on the owning item; Guidance for filing an item states which kinds are addition-safe, so an agent does not discover the constraint by failing a gate"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/goal","value":"explainable-graph"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/objective","value":"Associative growth is bounded by dilution rather than by count, so an honest sibling link is always recordable and a dilution pass is always refused"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/value","value":"Two declarations enforce the same intent with different strictness. The weaker-but-correct one measures dilution; the stronger one forbids a legitimate edit that dilutes nothing."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/impact","value":"Every future item that records a sibling relation trips a block gate, so the cheapest compliant response is to leave real context unrecorded or to mislabel it as a semantic kind."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/outcome","value":"Semantic share is the enforced quantity for composition; any raw associative count remains a reported diagnostic with declared headroom, never a zero-headroom block gate."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/why_now","value":"Hit immediately: filing four well-linked findings this session took related from 6,053 to 6,063 and turned two block gates red, with semantic share rising at the same time."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-96h7"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":95},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-1jzupz","kind":"implements","created_at":"2026-08-13T08:45:58.302Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-96h7","kind":"implements","created_at":"2026-08-13T08:45:58.302Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-j82fd3","kind":"implements","created_at":"2026-08-13T08:45:58.302Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-mfvsng","kind":"verifies","created_at":"2026-08-13T08:45:58.302Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-q6n8sj","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-08-13T08:45:58.302Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"8d21a585fb728522c9e5256735f8f35259bfa7fc6d0e2380f7c3f1eaa206037b","item_hash_version":2,"message":"File the zero-headroom related ceiling measured while filing this session's findings"}
{"ts":"2026-08-13T08:46:22.422Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"7ebf2cca0e1c37e7b3d988ef","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-hnc9w7","lineage:pm-hnc9w7","lineage:pm-a8zm","lineage:pm-6x7o","lineage:pm-96h7","lineage:pm-33cw","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"pm-hnc9w7","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-hnc9w7","lineage:pm-hnc9w7","lineage:pm-a8zm","lineage:pm-6x7o","lineage:pm-96h7","lineage:pm-33cw","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.229","source":"probe"}},"op":"update","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/body","value":"## The two declarations\n\nBoth live in the same registry and both descend from pm-q6n8sj, which correctly identified that `related` was the largest edge population and the only unbounded one.\n\n```\nrelated-to-ceiling         edges-related               ceiling 6053   block   owner pm-q6n8sj\n  negative_control: 6053 pass / 6054 fail\n  authorization_decision: pm-4jqm\n\nsemantic-edge-share-floor  semantic-edge-share-permille  floor 79     block   owner pm-q6n8sj\n  negative_control: 79 pass / 78 fail\n```\n\nThe share floor is the one that expresses the intent. It fails exactly when the fraction of traversable edges falls, which is the dilution pm-q6n8sj set out to prevent. It is indifferent to how large the graph gets, which is the correct indifference.\n\nThe raw ceiling is pinned to the count observed when it was declared. Its negative control states that one more associative row than existed at that instant is a failure.\n\n## What that means in practice\n\nFiling four findings this session, each with the associative sibling context an item is supposed to carry, took `edges-related` from 6,053 to 6,063. Both `graph-composition` and `tracker-context-quality` went to `verdict: block`.\n\nSemantic share over the same edit went from 81.0 to 81.2 permille against a floor of 79. The edit the raw ceiling refused was an edit that improved the quantity the project says it cares about.\n\nRetyping those ten rows to `implements`, `verifies` and `discovered_from` cleared both gates and moved semantic edges from 836 to 849 and share to 70.0 permille of total edges by the audit's own basis. That outcome is good, and it is the outcome the share floor would have produced on its own. The raw ceiling contributed nothing except the failure.\n\n## Why the incentive is wrong, not just inconvenient\n\nWith the ceiling at zero headroom, an agent recording two genuinely-associated items has three options: leave the relation unrecorded, spell it as a semantic kind it does not deserve, or fail the build. The second is the cheapest and the most damaging, and it is the precise failure mode the operating rules already warn about — a cue names a relation's kind and object, never its subject, so lexical promotion of associative links to semantic ones has already been measured at precision zero out of eight.\n\nA bound whose cheapest compliant response is mislabelling is worse than no bound.\n\n## Addition safety by kind, as currently declared\n\n| kind | bound | adding an edge |\n|---|---|---|\n| implements | floor 2591 | always safe |\n| discovered_from | floor 474 | always safe |\n| verifies | floor 245 | always safe |\n| supersedes | floor 84 | always safe |\n| blocked_by | none declared | safe |\n| related | ceiling 6053 | fails at any addition |\n| blocks | ceiling 243 | fails at any addition |\n\nOnly the two ceiling-bounded kinds are addition-unsafe, and both are pinned to their observation. `blocks` has an independent and deliberate rationale on pm-c90tfh — fabricated ordering edges are the specific harm there — so the two cases should be dispositioned separately rather than as one policy.\n\n## Boundary\n\nThis is not a request to raise the number. Raising a pinned ratchet by hand is the erosion these declarations exist to catch. The repair is to enforce composition and demote the raw count to reporting."},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-13T08:46:22.422Z"}],"before_hash":"8d21a585fb728522c9e5256735f8f35259bfa7fc6d0e2380f7c3f1eaa206037b","after_hash":"e4d30344b8f5a005db2ec180e200de454323e7a77198b8ab005d479e859ead25","item_hash_version":2,"message":"Record the two overlapping declarations and the observed sequence"}
